        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chip Zien, Stephen Sondheim, Willard Huyck, Lea Thompson, Jeffrey Jones, Tim Robbins\n- Works: Into the Woods, Howard the Duck\n- Roles: actor, composer, lyricist, film director\n- Awards: Academy Award, Tony Awards, Grammy Awards, Pulitzer Prize, Laurence Olivier Award, Presidential Medal of Freedom\n\nFacts:\n- Stephen Joshua Sondheim was born on March 22, 1930 and is an American composer and lyricist known for more than a half-century of contributions to musical theatre.\n- Jerome Herbert \"Chip\" Zien was born on March 20, 1947 and is an American actor.\n- In 1986, Howard the Duck, titled Howard: A New Breed of Hero in the UK, was released as an American science-fiction comedy film directed by Willard Huyck and starring Chip Zien, Lea Thompson, Jeffrey Jones, and Tim Robbins.\n- Chip Zien is best known for playing the lead role of the Baker in the original Broadway production of Into the Woods by Stephen Sondheim.\n- Stephen Sondheim has received an Academy Award, eight Tony Awards including a Special Tony Award for Lifetime Achievement in the Theatre, eight Grammy Awards, a Pulitzer Prize, a Laurence Olivier Award, and the 2015 Presidential Medal of Freedom.",
